6. EMITTER COVERAGE / SAFELIST (check 9, read not just log)
   tailwind.config.js content globs cover web/templates/**/*.html and
   web/static/js/**/*.js only — Go-source-only class literals
   (colorClass, successRateTextClass/BarClass, verdictClasses map) are
   NOT scanned and would otherwise be purged; the worker's safelist entry
   documents each source function and is current (grep confirms no
   Go-emitted color class is missing a matching safelist/scan entry, and
   emitter_coverage.py — independently re-read, logic is sound — reported
   clean on both my oracle runs).
   successRateBarClass (bg-lime-500 etc.) was left un-darkened: traced its
   only three call sites (whatif/monte-carlo.html) and confirmed it is a
   plain progress-bar FILL with no overlaid text — the 4.5:1 text
   criterion the ruling named does not apply to it, and it is not a
   template-content color-literal purge risk (present in the safelist).
   Judged correctly out of the darkening requirement's scope.

7. ACCESSIBILITY.md CONFORMANCE for all touched surfaces
   Point 7 (contrast, both themes): verified live per #4 above, plus the
   oracle's clean 9-page x 2-theme sweep for everything the sweep does
   reach.
   Point 12 (dark-mode parity): CSS-custom-property tokens flip
   automatically; verified no `dark:` twin needed and both themes clean.
   Point 8 (meaning not by color alone): renderError banners pair color
   with an icon (SVG alert glyph, aria-hidden) and the literal text
   "Error" — unchanged by this attempt, still present.
   No new hidden-text abuse, no new clickable div/span/tr introduced by
   this attempt (pre-existing onclick-div sites, e.g. KPI tiles, are
   unchanged carry-overs, U15's scope per SPEC.md — not this task's).

OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking, for the lead):
- Oracle gap: render_probe.js does not activate what-if tabs or open the
  dashboard's HTMX-loaded modals before its axe sweep, so the "9 pages x 2
  themes" claim is narrower than it reads for /whatif and /dashboard.
  I closed this gap manually this attempt (all clean); recommend folding
  tab-click + modal-open steps into render_probe.js itself so future edits
  to hidden-by-default content are caught mechanically, not by a checker's
  manual probe. This is a process/tooling finding, not an a11y defect —
  it does not change this PASS because the underlying rendered content was
  independently confirmed clean.
- Oracle flakiness under CPU contention (my first run's spurious FAIL) is
  worth a note for whoever runs accept.sh next: an unrelated concurrent
  `go build` can starve whatif-verify.sh's own build/start and produce a
  false ORACLE FAIL. Not a defect in U6's deliverable.
- successRateBarClass's un-darkened -500 fills are pre-existing and out of
  this attempt's explicitly named scope (text tiers only); no contrast
  violation found live, but a formal 3:1 non-text-contrast check was not
  run (WCAG 1.4.11 is largely a manual criterion axe does not fully
  cover). Candidate for a follow-up if the lead wants numeric coverage.
- All other findings in SPEC.md §10 (th scope, onclick-div sites, tab a11y
  cluster) are explicitly PRE-EXISTING / deferred to U15 per the rulings
  already on record; not re-litigated here.

